# Cursor Rules for Lethe
# Refer to AGENTS.md for full contributor and architectural guidelines.

- Adhere to the division of labor in AGENTS.md: owner hand-writes the batch loop, sqlsafe, guards, policy schema, and adapter extraction.
- Never write SQL using string concatenation with user input; always use parameterization and sqlsafe.
- Dry-run is the default; mutations require explicit --apply.
- Never log personal data or row contents (use log/slog with metadata only).
- Keep dependencies minimal (pgx/v5, goccy/go-yaml, google/uuid, stdlib flag, slog).
